 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 533809,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Do regular dodecagons (12-sided regular polygons) tessellate the plane by themselves?<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/957c8a36e65a1274.png\" alt=\"A tessellation pattern is made up of eight dodecagons and ten equilateral triangles.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>For regular polygons to be able to tesselate, the shapes must meet at a vertex so that the interior angles have a sum of 360°.</p>\n<p>A dodecagons has 12 sides, so <span data-math=\"n = 12\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The measure of each interior angle of a regular polygon with <i>n</i> sides is given by <span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{\\left( {n - 2} \\right)180^\\circ }}{n}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{\\left( {n - 2} \\right)180^\\circ }}{n} = \\frac{{\\left( {12 - 2} \\right)180^\\circ }}{{12}} = \\frac{{\\left( {10} \\right)180^\\circ }}{{12}} = \\frac{{1,080^\\circ }}{{12}} = 90^\\circ \"></span></p>\n<p>Since the interior angles of a dodecagon are integer factors of 360°, it makes tessellations within reach. However, dodecagons by themselves cannot tesselate. If you add equilateral triangles between them, they can fill the gaps.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Not by themselves, but by adding an equilateral triangle, the two regular polygons do tessellate the plane without gaps."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
